	(text_box "DESIGN NOTES:\nPYRO CONTINUITY - ADC SENSE \nDivider: 1.0 MΩ (top) / 150 kΩ (bottom) → ADC\nTest current (through igniter): ≈ 21 µA @ 24 V (safe, no ignition)\nADC voltage if igniter present: ≈ 3.1 V\nADC voltage if igniter open / missing: ≈ 0 V\nConditions (MOSFET OFF):\nIgniter connected → ADC ≈ 3.1 V → Continuity OK\nIgniter open / fuse blown → ADC ≈ 0 V → No continuity\nRMK :Continuity check valid only when MOSFET is OFF (during firing ADC goes low by design)."
